    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόερσε</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		aor. almost always in <i><span class="en">
			3
		</span></i> pers. (imper. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόερσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					110
				</span></i>
			):—<i>swept away,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα με κῦμ᾽ ἀπόερσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.348
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅν ῥά τ᾽ ἔναυλος ἀπο̄έρσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.283
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μιν ἀπο̄έρσειε μέγας
			ποταμός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				329
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπούρας.</span></div>
